WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:01.866
- Life is like a bunch of Korean snacks,

00:00:01.866 --> 00:00:03.825
you never know what you're
eating 'till you open it.

00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:06.545
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.545 --> 00:00:08.698
- It feels like Harry Potter having

00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:10.677
Bertie Bott beans for the first time.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.919
- This is the first time I'm like,

00:00:11.919 --> 00:00:13.405
"Oh, yeah, Korean food."

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:16.842
- Korean food for me would be,

00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:18.812
anything that has fins,

00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:21.300
or anything under the ocean.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.879
- If it says fun and yum on the packet,

00:00:22.879 --> 00:00:24.307
it has to be fun and yum, right?

00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:25.457
- That's (beep) good.

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:26.827
- A little bland.

00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:27.721
- Very bland.

00:00:27.721 --> 00:00:29.044
- There's no masala, there's no taste.

00:00:29.044 --> 00:00:31.285
- It tastes a little bit
like nothing, really.

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:32.759
- I don't generally like seafood,

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:34.803
but this is pretty tasty.

00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:36.486
- It's like just having fried flour.

00:00:36.486 --> 00:00:38.147
- This is peanut balls.

00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:40.746
And this is peanut balls icy.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:41.839
- How do you even know that?

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:43.824
- Because it says right here in English.

00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:45.796
- It is sweet on the inside.

00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:48.002
So I dunno why you call it spicy.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.407
- In India you get a peanut snack,

00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:52.357
then a spicy snack separately.

00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:53.652
But this is like--

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:54.552
- Mashed together.

00:00:54.552 --> 00:00:56.304
- It does the fusion
dance and mashes together,

00:00:56.304 --> 00:00:58.244
and then you get Korean food.

00:00:58.244 --> 00:00:59.265
- So among the two,

00:00:59.265 --> 00:01:01.204
I think that I can keep
on having for a long time.

00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:03.312
- Yeah, this is definitely better.

00:01:03.312 --> 00:01:04.582
- Not spicy, but the best flavor.

00:01:04.582 --> 00:01:05.709
- You know Sean,

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:07.090
this is like one of those chocolates

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.437
when you eat them, you
think it's really good,

00:01:08.437 --> 00:01:10.597
but after two bites you
don't wanna eat them.

00:01:10.597 --> 00:01:12.489
- We have crunchy rice rolls here,

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.624
which look a bit like
Rice Krispies Cereal Bars.

00:01:19.654 --> 00:01:21.742
Tastes exactly like Rice Krispies.

00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:24.215
Again, tasteless, it just has
a little hint of sweetness,

00:01:24.215 --> 00:01:25.597
and that's it.

00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:28.035
- I didn't really love
it, or I didn't hate it,

00:01:28.035 --> 00:01:29.799
it was fine, I could eat it.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:32.397
- Very mild and very light,

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:34.815
it's a good, sweet way to end a meal.

00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:37.900
- I would like to draw your
attention to the fact that

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.856
a kancho sample choco biscuit

00:01:39.856 --> 00:01:42.373
winks very suggestively at the user.

00:01:42.373 --> 00:01:43.906
- They know what they're doing.

00:01:43.906 --> 00:01:45.868
They get all loaded with sugary stuff,

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:47.599
like Indian and American snacks.

00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:50.074
- So it's chocolate inside a biscuit,

00:01:50.074 --> 00:01:51.243
and then you bite into it,

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.870
and the chocolate oozes out!

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.920
- Dude, none of that happened for me.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.733
- I love all of it, I mean--

00:01:57.733 --> 00:01:58.906
- Really, how?

00:01:58.906 --> 00:02:00.415
- Yeah, I did love it!

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.933
- I liked it, most of it.

00:02:03.933 --> 00:02:06.761
- The magic formula is, when in doubt,

00:02:06.761 --> 00:02:09.714
add two hundred grams of red chili powder.

00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:11.955
Which I think should be followed.

00:02:11.955 --> 00:02:16.955
(upbeat music)

